    {
      "title": "Three Options",
      "desc": "Offload, re-encrypt or pass through",
      "detail": "Offloading, as here, is simple and fast but leaves the inside traffic readable. Re-encrypting opens a second TLS connection from the proxy to the app server, so it stays encrypted inside too. Passing through forwards the TLS bytes without opening them: the certificate lives on the app servers, and the proxy can only choose a server by address and the name in the Client Hello, not by URL.",
      "facts": [
        [
          "Offload",
          "Plain HTTP inside"
        ],
        [
          "Re-encrypt",
          "TLS inside as well"
        ],
        [
          "Pass through",
          "Proxy can’t read it"
        ]
      ],
      "events": [
